148 0 obj
<<
/Title (One important issue in deep learning is the vanishing gradient problem. In deep networks, gradients can become very small as they are propagated backward through many layers. When this happens, early layers learn very slowly, and the network may fail to capture useful patterns. ReLU activation was used because it reduces this problem compared to sigmoid or tanh activations. Batch Normalization was also added because it stabilizes the distribution of layer inputs, supports faster convergence, and helps the model train more reliably.)
/Dest [10 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 126 0 R
/Next 160 0 R
>>
endobj
149 0 obj
<<
/Title (Self-attention is valuable because clinical notes are not always read in a simple left-to-right manner. A doctor may scan for key warning terms such as fever, hypotension, tachypnea,  altered mental status, infection, or oxygen desaturation. Transformer models use self-attention  to connect important words across the note and identify which terms contribute most to the classification decision.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 161 0 R
/Next 127 0 R
>>
endobj
